  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical assistance to EU Volunteers PEOPLE project by CRS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CRS&#x2019;s MEAL team will provide technical support on the development of the Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability and Learning (MEAL) plan and will be involved in the mid and end term evaluation of the programme. CRS is also responsible for delivering training and support on facilitation skills, volunteer motivation and management. CRS will support partners with the development of their volunteer management policies

This support is critical for the success of the project. It is also important for the partnership with CRS on capacity strengthening and their engagement in the project. 

This sum was included in the PEOPLE budget but is ineligible to submit to the donor as CRS are deemed by the EU as a different category of partner which cannot receive a grant.

CRS will be asked to draw up a budget for this amount.

50% to be transferred up front and the remaining 50% to be transferred upon receipt of a financial report for the first part of the budget and a cash forecast for the remaining funds.

See ICD974 for more information about the PEOPLE project</narrative>
  </description>
